  "description": "RAW Shimano\n\nThe RAW is a bike I’ve been looking forward to for a long time. It flies down the hills when fully loaded and I found myself sending it off drops in the trail even with my bike packing gear attached. It's beautifully balanced and far more capable off-road then my skills allow! The ride is super smooth and was really comfortable over the savage terrain of the HT550.\n\n- Josh Ibbett, ultra racer\n\nEvery MASON bicycle is built for adventures. But the RAW is the bicycle created for the biggest, roughest, most off-the-grid journeys on the planet.\n\nWith its flat bar layout and 120mm suspension fork, the RAW takes a mountain bike format and pushes it further: into the realms of bikepacking, adventure racing and remote exploration. Multiple equipment-mounting points enable the longest voyages, carrying fluids, food, and camping gear for the long haul, without compromising on serious off-road performance. Combining a custom mix of Dedacciai and Reynolds tubing, the RAW is built by hand in Scotland to exacting specifications. The latest update for 2025 future-proofs the RAW with MASON-designed UDH (Universal Derailleur Hanger) dropouts – designed carefully to open up a full choice of modern transmission specifications. Other updates include dedicated rack-mount eyelets at the base of the seat stays and a new colour choice: AccursedOchre.\n\nThe RAW is race-proven, with a record that includes the Atlas Mountain Race, the Silk Road Mountain Race and the Highland Trail 550. Race after race, it has delivered results for ultra racers taking on the biggest terrain with days’ or weeks’ worth of kit.\n\nThe RAW's Shimano options deliver the tried-and-tested workhorses of the SLX and XT groupsets, loved and trusted by mountain bikers everwhere. New for 2025, the addition of the Universal Derailleur Hanger standard maintains wide-open options for future component decisions.\n\nOur recommended fork is the Rockshox SID Ultimate. Well-balanced to cater for trail riding with 120mm travel and a 44mm offset, the SID Ultimate is packed in a stiff, lightweight 35mm chassis, and is equipped with the top of the line Charger Race Day damper and bolt-on arch mounted mudguard.\n\nFinishing off the build, a Hunt Trailwide V2 wheelset provides optimal toughness and ride quality, while other options are available too.\n\nRockshox SID Ultimate fork, with 120mm travel and 44mm offset\n\nProvisions for bolt-on top tube bag and ample full frame bag space with with opened-out front triangle.\n\nPremium quality ‘black stainless’ bolt and fittings set.\n\nMASON ‘Element’ 3D printed TPU chainstay protector.\n\nPNW Loam 31.6 dropper post.\n\nChoice of Schwalbe, Maxxis or Vittoria 29” tyres in various widths and tread patterns\n\nFabrication and wet-painting by Scottish-based Five Land Bikes, as well as eCoat corrosion treatment inside and out.\n\n29” Hunt Trailwide V2 Wheelset\n\nRenthal Fatbar\n\nDeda EC/ZS44mm sealed bearing headset\n\nErgon GA2 lock on grips\n\nRitchey WCS trail stem (Length as per customer request)\n\nFizik Terra Argo X3 Kium railed saddle",
